INT. ST. ANSELM HOSPITAL - LEAD-LINED X-RAY VAULT - NIGHT

Concrete. A heavy door. A humming machine. One red lamp.

BILLIE FROST, 20s, nurse, lead apron, holds a clipboard against her chest. OSWIN PARR, 80s, patient on the table, in a gown, hands folded. He hasn't blinked in a minute.

Billie checks the film. Oswin watches her check.

BILLIE
Almost done, Mr. Parr.

He nods. The machine hums. She steps behind the glass. Presses the button. A flash.

On the monitor: his ribcage, his spine. And behind the ribs, something curled. Dark. Furred.

Billie freezes. Oswin turns his head toward the glass. He smiles with all his teeth.

The lamp flickers. She backs toward the door. He sits up. They both lunge for the handle. Her hand lands first. The door will not turn.

Oswin slides off the table. Calm. Unhurried. She throws her shoulder against the steel. He puts a hand on her arm, gently.

OSWIN
Don't be frightened, dear.

She stops. His thumb strokes her wrist. The red lamp goes out.
